---
import ReynoldsLayout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const lastUpdated = '10 August 2026';
---

<ReynoldsLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Reynolds Dryline Personal Data Use"
  description="Read how Reynolds Dryline collects, uses and protects personal data from website enquiries and careers applications in Leicestershire, UK today."
  canonical="https://www.reynoldsdryline.co.uk/privacy"
>
  <PageHero
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="How we collect, use and protect personal information."
    breadcrumb="Legal"
  />

  <section class="rd-section rd-section--surface px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-gray">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 !mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website is operated by <strong>L. Reynolds (Building Systems) Limited</strong>, trading as
        <strong>Reynolds Dryline</strong> (“we”, “us”, “our”).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Registered address:</strong><br />
        9 Quorn Business Quarter, Loughborough Road, Mountsorrel, Leicestershire, LE12 7XF, United Kingdom
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Privacy contact:</strong><br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@reynoldsltd.co.uk">info@reynoldsltd.co.uk</a><br />
        Telephone: <a href="tel:01509816600">01509 816 600</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        We are the data controller for personal information collected through this website
        (www.reynoldsdryline.co.uk).
      </p>

      <h2>2. What information we collect</h2>
      <h3>Contact enquiries</h3>
      <p>
        When you use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a> we collect the details you submit, which may include:
        first name, last name, company, email address, phone number, project type and message content.
      </p>

      <h3>Careers and applications</h3>
      <p>
        When you use our <a href="/careers">careers form</a> we collect the details you submit, which may include:
        name, email, phone number, position applied for, experience, cover letter/message, CV upload, and your
        recruitment consent confirmation.
      </p>

      <h3>Website and technical data</h3>
      <p>
        When you browse the site we may process technical information such as IP address, browser type,
        device information, pages visited and approximate location derived from IP. Analytics tools only run
        if you accept analytics cookies — see our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Cookie consent preferences</h3>
      <p>
        We store your cookie choices (essential always on; analytics on/off) in your browser so we can
        remember them on return visits.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Why we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to project enquiries and general contact requests</li>
        <li>To process job and subcontractor applications and manage recruitment</li>
        <li>To operate, secure and improve this website</li>
        <li>To measure site usage where you have consented to analytics</li>
        <li>To comply with legal or regulatory obligations</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

      <h2>4. Lawful bases</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR we rely on one or more of the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — responding to business enquiries and running a secure website
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Consent</strong> — analytics cookies, and retention of application details for future
          opportunities where you have agreed on the careers form
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal obligation</strong> — where we must keep records to meet the law
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Who we share information with</h2>
      <p>We may share personal information with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Netlify</strong> — website hosting and form processing for contact and careers submissions
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dotwall</strong> — website analytics/monitoring, only if you accept analytics cookies
        </li>
        <li>
          Professional advisers or authorities where required by law
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some providers may process data outside the UK. Where that happens, we expect appropriate safeguards
        to be in place (for example standard contractual clauses or equivalent protections used by the provider).
      </p>

      <h2>6. How long we keep information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact enquiries</strong> — kept for as long as needed to deal with your enquiry and any
          follow-up, then deleted or anonymised unless we need to keep them longer for legal reasons
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Careers applications</strong> — kept for the recruitment process; if you consent on the form,
          we may retain details to contact you about future roles
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics data</strong> — retained according to the analytics provider’s settings and your
          consent choice
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
        <li>Ask us to correct inaccurate data</li>
        <li>Ask us to delete your data in certain circumstances</li>
        <li>Restrict or object to certain processing</li>
        <li>Data portability, where applicable</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent where we rely on consent (for example analytics or future-role retention)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise these rights, contact
        <a href="mailto:info@reynoldsltd.co.uk">info@reynoldsltd.co.uk</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO):
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal information.
        No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, but we work with established
        hosting and form providers to reduce risk.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website is aimed at business users and job applicants. We do not knowingly collect personal
        data from children.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Related policies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a></li>
        <li><a href="/contact">Contact us</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top of this
        page shows when it was last revised.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ReynoldsLayout>
